# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets redirect rules.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/redirects/
#
# IMPORTANT: CF allows only ONE `*` splat per pattern and silently DROPS a rule
# that breaks it. `:splat` in the destination is what carries the rest of the
# path across — without it, /genova/calendar/ lands at the region's feed instead
# of its calendar. redirect-rules.test.ts fails the build if either regresses.
#
# Rules are matched in order, most specific first.

# These were English addresses, so they move to where English lives now. The
# /it/ and /ru/ twins below already named their language and are unchanged.
#
# The city URLs the site shipped with for a few hours, before the slice became
# the region. A browser that saw "/" 301 to "/genova/" cached that answer
# forever, so these keep resolving. Now that a region feed can be filtered to a
# city, the legacy city FEED lands on that filter (?city=…); the exact feed rules
# come first so they win over the splat below. The city sub-pages (calendar/map,
# which don't filter by city) still land on the region's sub-page via the splat.
/genova/         /en/liguria/genova/           301
/milano/         /en/lombardia/milano/         301
/torino/         /en/piemonte/torino/          301
/it/genova/      /it/liguria/genova/        301
/ru/genova/      /ru/liguria/genova/        301
/genova          /en/liguria/genova/           301
/milano          /en/lombardia/milano/         301
/torino          /en/piemonte/torino/          301
/it/genova       /it/liguria/genova/        301
/ru/genova       /ru/liguria/genova/        301
/genova/*        /en/liguria/:splat            301
/milano/*        /en/lombardia/:splat          301
/torino/*        /en/piemonte/:splat           301
/it/genova/*     /it/liguria/:splat         301
/ru/genova/*     /ru/liguria/:splat         301

# The bare paths — "/", "/calendar", "/map" and their language-prefixed twins —
# are deliberately absent. They name neither a language nor a region, and both
# have to be chosen per reader: the language from Accept-Language, the region
# from where the reader is or where the events are. A rule here can read nothing
# and so sent every visitor to one region, the one the site was founded in, long
# after the site had stopped being about it. See src/lib/i18n/bare-entry.ts.

# @astrojs/sitemap wrote this file until the page tier was enumerated by hand.
# Nothing indexes it any more, and Google has read it for two months, so it
# moves rather than disappears.
/sitemap-0.xml   /sitemap-pages.xml         301
